BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:📢 Piccadilly: Piccadilly line service control staff are plannin
 g to take strike action from Friday 20…
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20261120T115900
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20261121T203000
DTSTAMP:20261116T000000Z
UID:c04cc63d6069fa2997f7@tfl-closures
CATEGORIES:Update from TfL's live status (not in the planned closures list
 )
DESCRIPTION:📢 Update from TfL's live status (not in the planned closure
 s list)\n\nTUBE STRIKE: Piccadilly line service control staff are planning
  to take strike action from Friday 20 until Saturday evening 21 November. 
 Piccadilly line customers should complete journeys by 1030 on Friday morni
 ng as service will begin to reduce after this time. There will be no servi
 ce from midday on Friday until Saturday evening\, including Night Tube on 
 Friday night. Normal Night Tube service is expected to operate on Saturday
  night. Due to shared infrastructure around the Ealing Common District lin
 e depot\, there will be no DISTRICT LINE service between Earls Court and R
 ichmond / Ealing Broadway from midday on Friday until Saturday evening. Re
 placement buses will operate during Friday Night Tube hours and Saturday d
 aytime only. Please use ELIZABETH LINE services for travel between Central
  London and Heathrow\, and METROPOLITAN LINE services between Rayners Lane
  and Uxbridge.\n\nFrom TfL's live status (Planned Closure)\, checked 19 No
 vember 2026.\n\nPlans can change. Check before you travel: https://tfl.gov
 .uk/tube-dlr-overground/status/\nPowered by TfL Open Data\nUnofficial cale
 ndar\, not produced or endorsed by Transport for London.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://tfl.gov.uk/tube-dlr-overground/status/
X-MICROSOFT-CDO-BUSYSTATUS:FREE
END:VEVENT
